  "body": "**What is this feature?**\n\nNumberInput no longer clamps an out of range value on the 500ms typing debounce. In-range values still update after that debounce so panel options can preview. Out of range values stay as typed until blur or Enter, then we clamp, show an error that stays until the next edit, and keep the allowed min/max visible.\n\n**Why do we need this feature?**\n\nTyping something like `-9` in Text size (min 1) showed an error for only 500ms, then the value jumped. That fails WCAG 2.2.1 (enough time): users who need more time never see the message, and a slow typist can have an intermediate value rewritten while they are still editing.\n\n**Who is this feature for?**\n\nKeyboard and screen reader users, and anyone who types slowly in panel number options.\n\n**Which issue(s) does this PR fix?**:\n\nFixes #109013\n\n**Special notes for your reviewer:**\n\n- In-range debounce is unchanged for live preview.\n- Clamp and `onChange` of the corrected value happen on blur or Enter.\n- Range text is always under the input when min/max are set (also used in the error and `aria-describedby` when valid).\n\nPlease check that:\n- [ ] It works as expected from a user's perspective.\n- [ ] If this is a pre-GA feature, it is behind a feature toggle.\n- [ ] The docs are updated, and if this is a [notable improvement](https://grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/contribute/release-notes/#how-to-determine-if-content-belongs-in-whats-new), it's added to our [What's New](https://grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/contribute/release-notes/) doc.",
  "changed_files": 4,
